12. Data Quality Notes
The initial review of the source tables identified the following
characteristics:
- Duplicate identifiers/records were found in orders and
  customers; deduplication was applied for the relevant analyses.
- Missing values in orders have different meanings. For example, a
  missing delivery_time_min is expected for a cancelled order.
- Missing values were found in customers.age and customers.gender.
- Casing differences and extra spaces occurred in categorical fields,
  including payment methods and city names.
- Negative values occurred in orders.discount_uah; this must be
  considered when checking order-total calculations.
- Some orders did not have a matching weather record. A LEFT JOIN
  preserves those orders in the analysis.
- A statistical outlier is not automatically an invalid record and
  should not be removed without further investigation.
